- op: create  # f580
  at: '2026-10-11T21:53:57Z'  # f580
  by: agent  # f580
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f580
  clock: 1  # f580
  nonce: f580  # f580
  data:  # f580
    kind: invariant  # f580
    title: "A taint file declaring provenance: community, named by --taint-* flag or claims-file extra_catalogs, loads as YOURS: its sanitizer clears a flow, --no-default-overlays keeps it, yet tiers lists it as community"  # f580
    status: violated  # f580
    priority: 2  # f580
    parent:  # f580
    tags:  # f580
    - catalogue  # f580
    - adr_0061  # f580
    - taint  # f580
    isbefore: []  # f580
    duplicate_of: []  # f580
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f580
    pr_ref:  # f580
    description: "Found 2026-10-11, investigating a residual the INV-dozav fixer (PR #1540) reported.\n\nADR-0061 ruling 3: \"The loader reads the tier from that line, never from the directory.\" Ruling 2: a community sanitizer never makes a verdict cleaner. Ruling 5: \"--no-default-overlays omits community rows from every family, taint included.\" The I/O-overlay family obeys all three for a file passed by flag or claims file (INV-kobam #1533, INV-dozav #1540), and the taint CHANNELS (taint_*.d/) do too. The taint FLAG and CLAIMS-FILE paths do not.\n\nROOT CAUSE (taint.py `load_taint_catalog_with_user_extras`, ~2299-2420): `channel_*_paths` are partitioned by `_declares_community_file` into the community layer vs the yours layer, but `cli_*_paths` (--taint-sources/--taint-sinks/--taint-sanitizers) and `extra_*_paths` (claims-file `extra_catalogs: sources/sinks/sanitizers`) go straight into `claims_layer`/`cli_layer`, whose sanitizers are stamped `user_supplied=True` and never `community=True`. `include_community` (the --no-default-overlays switch) is never consulted for them. Meanwhile `catalogue_tiers` reads the provenance line and lists the same file under `tiers.community`.\n\nREPRO (dev 020b5bd7ce): repo/app.py `key = os.urandom(32); wrapped = mylib.wrap(key); open(\"out.bin\",\"wb\").write(wrapped)`; san_community.yaml = `provenance: community`, `retrieved: 2026-01-01`, transform key_material->wrapped_key via python `mylib.wrap`; claim taint_flow source_taint key_material, prohibited_sink_zone host_fs.\n\n| load path | exit | verdict | caveats | tiers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| no sanitizer | 1 | violated | - | - |\n| --taint-sanitizers san_community.yaml | 3 | confirmed_with_caveats | user_supplied_sanitizer | community |\n| same + --no-default-overlays | 3 | confirmed_with_caveats | user_supplied_sanitizer | community |\n| claims-file extra_catalogs.sanitizers | 3 | confirmed_with_caveats | user_supplied_sanitizer | community |\n| same + --no-default-overlays | 3 | confirmed_with_caveats | user_supplied_sanitizer | community |\n| CONTROL: XDG taint_sanitizers.d/ copy | 1 | violated | withheld_community_sanitizer | community |\n| CONTROL: channel + --no-default-overlays | 1 | violated | - | community |\n\nSo a community sanitizer clears the flow (violated -> confirmed_with_caveats) when named by flag or claims file, survives --no-default-overlays, and the text report lists the file only under \"USER-SUPPLIED catalogue input ... [CLI flag]\" while the JSON lists it under tiers.community -- text and JSON disagree about its tier, and the treatment matches neither the ADR nor the I/O family.\n\nSources and sinks from such a file only add, so for them the effect is limited to --no-default-overlays not omitting them and a community sink/source acting at user precedence (it can REPLACE a shipped entry on (module, name, kind) -- a displacement -- where the community layer may only add).\n\nFix direction: partition cli_*/extra_* paths by `_declares_community_file` exactly as the channels are -- community ones join the community layer (sanitizers stamped community=True and withheld; sources/sinks add-only; whole layer dropped when include_community is False, and disclosed as omitted like `omitted_community_overlays`). Then text and JSON report the same tier. Also fix spec docs/hypergumbo-spec.md's ADR-0061 status table: \"The other families' user channels do not read it yet\" is stale for the taint channels and should name this flag/claims-file gap until fixed."  # f580
    fields:  # f580
      statement: "A taint file's tier is its provenance line whatever path loaded it: a community file named by flag or claims file only adds, its sanitizers are withheld, --no-default-overlays omits it, and text and JSON report the same tier."  # f580
      root_cause: "load_taint_catalog_with_user_extras partitions only the taint_*.d channel paths by provenance; cli_* and extra_* paths go straight into user layers stamped user_supplied and never consult include_community."  # f580
